<td id="S4.T1.2.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.75</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">0.81</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.55</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.9.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.55</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours with K=3 (Layers 7, 15, and 22)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.10.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.83</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.10.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.91</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.10.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.95</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.10.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.96</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>
AUROC (<math id="S4.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>) results for EYE-LLaMA and MentaLLaMA on both OOD datasets. Best results are in bold.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.04655v1/images/main_plots.png" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/90;" width="476" height="90" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Comparison of ROC curves for OOD Detection with the single <math id="S4.F3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value baselines across layers.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.04655v1/images/false_alarm_0.5.png" id="S4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/83;" width="476" height="83" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>False Alarm Rate Guarantees Plots: False alarm is upper bounded by <math id="S4.F4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> on average in most test cases.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.6 </span>Ablation Studies</h3>

<div id="S4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform the following studies relevant to the proposed Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 OOD Detection for Specialized LLMs ‣ Polysemantic Dropout: Conformal OOD Detection for Specialized LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1. Choice of the Valid Merging Function:</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in <a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3 Combining hypothesis ‣ 2 Background ‣ Polysemantic Dropout: Conformal OOD Detection for Specialized LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>, different valid merging functions can be used to combine the <math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values. We use Arithmetic Mean on <math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values from the three layers (<math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>22</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22</annotation></semantics></math>) for reporting the results in Section <a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Polysemantic Dropout: Conformal OOD Detection for Specialized LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>. We also experiment with the other three functions and report the AUROC results in <a href="#S4.T2" title="In 1. Choice of the Valid Merging Function: ‣ 4.6 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Polysemantic Dropout: Conformal OOD Detection for Specialized LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We observe that Arithmetic Mean performs the best with comparable performance by Geometric Mean. Performance by all the functions is comparable in the case of MentaLLaMA. ROC curves for the other three valid merging functions (with similar performance as Arithmetic Mean) are included in the Appendix.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:60.6pt;vertical-align:-28.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-35.9pt,6.3pt) scale(0.827589993409637,0.827589993409637) ;">
<table id="S4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EYE-LLaMA</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"></th>
